        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "## Problem Statement\n**Exercise 1**:  \nFor the function  \n\n\\[\nf(x)=x^{2}+2x+1,\n\\]\n\ndetermine  \n\n1. the *derivative* \\(f'(x)\\),  \n2. the **indefinite integral** \\(\\displaystyle \\int f(x)\\,dx\\).\n\n### Solution\n1. Derivative  \n   \\[\n   f'(x)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\bigl(x^{2}+2x+1\\bigr)=2x+2.\n   \\]\n\n2. Integral  \n   \\[\n   \\int f(x)\\,dx\n     =\\int \\bigl(x^{2}+2x+1\\bigr)\\,dx\n     =\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+x^{2}+x+C,\n   \\]\n   where \\(C\\) is the constant of integration.\n\n---\n\n## Linear Algebra at a Glance\nConsider the matrix  \n\n\\[\nA=\\begin{pmatrix}a & b \\\\[4pt] c & d\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\n- Determinant  \n  \\[\n  \\det(A)=ad-bc.\n  \\]\n\n- Trace  \n  \\[\n  \\operatorname{tr}(A)=a+d.\n  \\]\n\n- Inverse (when \\(ad-bc\\neq0\\))  \n\n  \\[\n  A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{ad-bc}\\begin{pmatrix}d & -b \\\\[4pt] -c & a\\end{pmatrix}.\n  \\]\n\n---\n\n## Real-World Connection\n> **Note**: In economics, a *cost function* \\(C(q)=100+5q\\) tells us that  \n> • Fixed cost = \\$100  \n> • Variable cost = \\$5 per unit of output \\(q\\).\n\nFor a purchase of 10 units:\n- Fixed cost: \\$100  \n- Variable cost: \\(5\\times10=\\$50\\)\n\nHence the **total cost** is  \n\n\\[\n100+50=\\boxed{\\$150}.\n\\]",
